    groups: 1-4 groups (one per legend entry), each sharing cap color K and fill color F
    bars_per_group: 2-3
    fill_color: F != K, F != bg; same F for all bars in a group; F may differ across groups
    columns: each bar occupies one column; no column shared between groups; min spacing >= 1 col
    bars and legend may share a column if legend block is above and separated by >= 1 bg row
  transform:
    for each legend entry (K, k), find bars capped by K
    rank bars by fill length descending (longest=rank 1)
    recolor the rank-k bar's fill cells to K (cap color replaces fill color)
generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are easy to satisfy constructively)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid width 10-20, height fixed 10. Choose 1-4 cap colors and assign each a fill color (all distinct, no overlap).
    2. Build legend at top-left: for each cap color K, place k cells of K vertically from row 0 in consecutive columns (with optional 1-col bg gap).
    3. For each group, choose 2-3 distinct fill lengths (1 to 8, must fit in rows below the bar's top cap which must be >= row 1). Place bars in available columns (>= 1 col apart, no group overlap). All bars bottom at row 9.
    4. Pick rank k per legend entry: 1 <= k <= bars_in_group. Set legend depth to k.
    5. Fill each bar column: cap color at top and row 9, fill color in between.
    6. Verify legend column does not conflict with bar pixels (legend occupies top rows, bar starts below with bg gap).
